      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page (titled \u0022Guarded Write Journal\u0022) describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**.\n\nSpecifically, it explains that:\n\n- Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or a record that it didn\u0027t exist \u2014 into an in-memory write journal.\n- If an agent run fails (due to turn cap, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order: restoring previous content for files that existed and deleting newly created files.\n- This gives each run all-or-nothing semantics for its writes without needing a database transaction \u2014 the journal itself acts as the transaction log, stored in process memory for the duration of one run.\n- The Query agent never uses the rollback functionality since it has no write capability.",
